"Cut the strip into four equal parts.": "3849931c7d98",
"Here is the problem. The denominator is not a count of things; it is the name of the piece. A half and a third are different sizes, the way a quarter and a dime are different coins. One quarter and one dime are two coins, but they are not two quarters. In the same way, one half and one third are two pieces, but they are not two fifths. You can only count pieces together when they are the same size.": "8da30c7510e5",
"How do you add 1/2 + 1/3 correctly?": "01f74300dd6e",
"In 3/4, the denominator is 4.": "d0a9ded0bd10",
"In 3/4, the numerator is 3.": "c203e6c2d551",
"One and one fourth is a mixed number.": "1f896a870344",
"One half and two fourths are equivalent fractions.": "fc084fac36be",
"One half is a fraction.": "3ba6780f7a60",
"Six is a common denominator for halves and thirds.": "c0185ffd6b0c",
"So make them the same size. Cut each half into three smaller pieces and each third into two. Now both strips are cut into sixths. One half is the same amount as three sixths, and one third is the same as two sixths. Fractions that have the same value are called equivalent fractions. Now the pieces match, and counting is easy: three sixths plus two sixths is five sixths. The smallest number of pieces that works for both, here six, is called the least common denominator.": "ecdad5ceccc2",
"Start with what a fraction means. The bottom number, the denominator, tells how many equal parts the whole has been divided into. The top number, the numerator, tells how many of those parts you have. So 1/2 means one of two equal pieces, and 1/3 means one of three. In English you say the top number first, “one half,” “one third,” “three fourths.” In Chinese you say the bottom number first: er fen zhi yi, two parts, take one.": "33088722abd9",
"There is a quick way to catch the mistake, even without cutting anything. When you add two amounts, the answer has to be bigger than each of them. One U.S. standard asks students to recognize that 2/5 + 1/2 = 3/7 must be wrong, because 3/7 is less than 1/2. Adding the tops and the bottoms always gives an answer that lands between the two fractions, never above them. If your sum is smaller than one of its parts, go back and cut again.": "987e257c83f1",
"Two halves make one whole.": "2395f21c7b44",
"What do the denominator and the numerator of a fraction tell you?": "7f8edc1dab99",
"When the pieces are already the same size, adding is simple. One fourth plus two fourths is three fourths: you just add the number of pieces, and the denominator stays the same, because the size of each piece does not change. Americans often call fourths “quarters,” so this also reads as one quarter plus two quarters equals three quarters. Sometimes the answer is more than a whole: three fourths plus one half is five fourths, which is one and one fourth. That is a mixed number, a whole number together with a fraction.": "683ac4f74059",
"Why is 2/5 not the answer to 1/2 + 1/3?": "7f541f4457ef",
"You eat one half of a pizza, and your friend eats one third of another pizza of the same size. How much pizza did you eat together? A quick answer is to add the tops and the bottoms: 1 + 1 = 2 and 2 + 3 = 5, so 1/2 + 1/3 = 2/5. It looks neat, but it cannot be right. Two fifths is less than one half. You added food and somehow ended up with less than you started with. Something has gone wrong, and this lesson finds out what.": "95c7fecb1352",
